WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.360
Movie

00:01.360 --> 00:07.140
My first lesson on the periodic table. Have you ever wondered what makes up the world around you?

00:08.620 --> 00:13.100
Everything you see touch and even eat comes from the periodic table of elements

00:13.800 --> 00:16.280
This fascinating tool is more than just a chart

00:16.440 --> 00:24.200
It's a systematic way that scientists organize all known elements these elements you see are the building blocks of everything in the universe

00:25.040 --> 00:31.660
From the air we breathe to the stars that twinkle in the night sky all can be found on the periodic table

00:32.320 --> 00:37.540
The periodic table is like a giant puzzle where each piece is a unique element with its own story

00:38.160 --> 00:41.220
Imagine if you were an explorer discovering new lands

00:41.960 --> 00:46.240
Each element in the periodic table is like a new land waiting to be explored

00:47.280 --> 00:52.920
Every element possesses unique characteristics just like different places have unique sights and sounds

00:53.680 --> 00:58.000
Take gold for instance a shiny element that we love to wear as jewelry or

00:58.360 --> 01:05.560
Helium the light is air gas that makes our balloons float and let's not forget oxygen the life-giving element

01:05.560 --> 01:07.560
We breathe in every second

01:07.640 --> 01:12.920
Just like explorers scientists are always on the lookout for new elements to add to our periodic table

01:13.040 --> 01:18.360
Now how do scientists keep track of all these elements? That's where the periodic table comes in

01:19.280 --> 01:25.360
Just like a librarian organizes books the periodic table arranges elements based on their properties

01:25.880 --> 01:29.480
Picture a neighborhood where houses on the same street share similar features

01:30.120 --> 01:32.240
That's how the periodic table works

01:33.240 --> 01:38.800
Elements in the same column have shared characteristics like helium and neon being non-reactive

01:39.520 --> 01:42.240
So you see the periodic table isn't just a chart

01:42.400 --> 01:48.760
It's a treasure map to the elements each element on the periodic table has a fascinating story to tell

01:49.840 --> 01:51.840
Let's take helium for example

01:52.240 --> 01:55.360
Did you know it was first discovered on the Sun not on earth?

01:55.920 --> 02:02.160
Talk about a hot discovery and then there's gold a precious metal that has been treasured by

02:02.440 --> 02:07.480
Civilizations for thousands of years its lustrous beauty has made it a symbol of wealth and power

02:08.200 --> 02:13.800
Who knows maybe one day you'll discover a new element and add your own story to the periodic table

02:14.240 --> 02:20.100
The periodic table is not just a tool for scientists. It's a gateway to understanding our universe

02:20.400 --> 02:22.400
It's like a secret code

02:22.640 --> 02:25.040
unlocking the mysteries of everything we know and see

02:25.720 --> 02:32.480
from the oxygen we breathe to the nitrogen that helps plants grow to the neon and glowing city lights and

02:33.000 --> 02:35.440
Even to the iron at the heart of distant stars

02:35.440 --> 02:43.440
So the next time you look at the periodic table remember, it's not just a chart. It's a universe waiting to be explored

